body:
I considered this already, and I come to the same conclusion I came to [last time](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105701#discussion_r2057808362).

Reducing to a single "Hint_Blit_Source" token would require the ShaderCompiler to more intelligently process that Hint Token. The relevant code is in Shader_compiler.cpp, Lines 948-958

```
} else if (u.hint == ShaderLanguage::ShaderNode::Uniform::HINT_BLIT_SOURCE) {
	name = "source";
} else if (u.hint == ShaderLanguage::ShaderNode::Uniform::HINT_BLIT_SOURCE2) {
	name = "source2";
} else if (u.hint == ShaderLanguage::ShaderNode::Uniform::HINT_BLIT_SOURCE3) {
	name = "source3";
} else if (u.hint == ShaderLanguage::ShaderNode::Uniform::HINT_BLIT_SOURCE4) {
	name = "source4";
} else {
	name = _mkid(vnode->name); //texture, use as is
}
```

A hypothetical reduction would still have to look like

```
} else if (u.hint == ShaderLanguage::ShaderNode::Uniform::HINT_BLIT_SOURCE) {
	switch(BlitHintsSoFar):
		case 0:
			name = "source";
			break;
		case 1:
			name = "source2";
			break;
		case 2: 
			name = "source3";
			break;
		case 3:
			name = "source4";
			break;
		default:
			name = "source";
}
```

The trouble comes in tracking the context of BlitHintsSoFar (how many HINT_BLIT_SOURCE have already counted) and passing it into `ShaderCompiler::_dump_node_code()`, which as I understand wants to parse individual nodes/line of GDShader code to deterministically produce GLSL code, without a lot (or any?) context about the other nodes/lines?

